                {
                    "no": 9,
                    "code": "Disneyland Resort Tickets - Theme Park Reservation Availability",
                    "description": "Disneyland Resort Tickets - Theme Park Reservation Availability",
                    "note": "Know Before You Go! To enter a Disneyland Park, both a valid Disney Ticket and \na date specific theme park reservation are now required. You must check there is \nsatisfactory availability in the parks for your chosen holiday dates before you \nbook your tickets. Tickets are non-refundable, so if you are not able to confirm \nyour chosen date after purchase, we will not be able to refund the ticket amount. \nDisney's Park Pass availability can be found here: \nhttps://disneyland.disney.go.com/availability-calendar/ Be aware that availability \ncan change and entry into a park on a given date cannot be guaranteed until you \nhave linked your tickets to your My Disney Experience account and made your \npark selections using Disney's Park Pass System. An alphanumeric ticket reference\nwill be generated in your Manage My Booking, approximately 30 days after paying\nfor your tickets in full. Link your tickets to your My Disney Experience account \nusing the reference found on your tickets. Some experiences may be modified or \nunavailable. For more information, along with health and safety measures, visit \nthe Disneyland California Know Before You Go site: \nhttps://disneyland.disney.go.com/experience-updates/Code.​​",
                    "dateModified": "2022-06-29T11:37:01",
                    "external": true,
                    "internal": true,
                    "priority": "H",
                    "itemInfo": [
                        "FLT 27",
